We recommend printing the sherBLOCK using high-quality ASA filament. Several free slicers are available online to process the files for printing. 

Within the slicer, make sure to immport all parts of the enclosure and move them within the printable area. Then, rotate the lid of the sherBLOCK so that the bottom is facing up; this is to ensure that the fine details where the two parts meet will be printed in the same axis. 

Adjusting the slicer print settings:
* Wall loops: 5 
* Top and bottom shell layers: 4
* Top and bottom shell thickness: 0.8mm
* Infill pattern: gyroid
* infill density: 15% 
* Pattern: gyroid 
* Initial layer speed: 35 mm/s
* Support: Tree (organic)
* Outer brim: 6mm
